<MATH_0002>-category with <MATH_0003>-fibre products. Explicitly, it follows
from the following chain of equivalences:
<STRUCT_0001>
<STRUCT_0002>{X} <STRUCT_0003>_{(<STRUCT_0004>{X} <STRUCT_0005>_<STRUCT_0006>{Y} <STRUCT_0007>{X})}
(<STRUCT_0008>{U} <STRUCT_0009>_<STRUCT_0010>{V} <STRUCT_0011>{U})
& =
<STRUCT_0012>{X} <STRUCT_0013>_{(<STRUCT_0014>{X} <STRUCT_0015>_<STRUCT_0016>{Y} <STRUCT_0017>{X})}
((<STRUCT_0018>{X} <STRUCT_0019>_<STRUCT_0020>{Y} <STRUCT_0021>{V})
<STRUCT_0022>_<STRUCT_0023>{V} (<STRUCT_0024>{X} <STRUCT_0025>_<STRUCT_0026>{Y} <STRUCT_0027>{V})) \\
& =
<STRUCT_0028>{X} <STRUCT_0029>_{(<STRUCT_0030>{X} <STRUCT_0031>_<STRUCT_0032>{Y} <STRUCT_0033>{X})}
(<STRUCT_0034>{X} <STRUCT_0035>_<STRUCT_0036>{Y} <STRUCT_0037>{X}
<STRUCT_0038>_<STRUCT_0039>{Y} <STRUCT_0040>{V}) \\
& =
<STRUCT_0041>{X} <STRUCT_0042>_<STRUCT_0043>{Y} <STRUCT_0044>{V} = <STRUCT_0045>{U}
<STRUCT_0046>
see
Lemmas <REF_0001> and
